Description: scaleplex_inlineass: pending queue survives probe->live rebind
 Patch 0101 added a pre-graph pending-chunk queue so sidecar SRT cues
 (decoded on a separate fast input demuxer that EOFs before the video
 filter graph is configured) survive long enough to be replayed at
 link_graph time. That worked for the simple case where
 configure_filtergraph runs once. It silently breaks when
 configure_filtergraph runs TWICE (probe pass + live pass under
 jellyfin 7.x's split-thread filter scheduler).
 .
 Failure trace (sidecar SRT + HW-decode-text-burn, captured 2026-05-26
 on the orthogonal-detector HW-text refactor branch):
 .
   1. Probe configure_filtergraph runs. link_graph binds flt_ctx1,
      drains pending into flt_ctx1's libass track. handle_subtitle
      switches to the fast (immediate-dispatch) path -- chunks bypass
      the pending queue and feed flt_ctx1 directly. By the time the
      sidecar SRT demuxer EOFs, every cue lives in flt_ctx1's track,
      and the pending queue is empty.
   2. Probe->live re-entry. flt_ctx1 is destroyed; the
      inlineass_filter_uninit_cb clears flt_ctx. link_graph binds the
      new graph's flt_ctx2. pending_count == 0 -> drain is a no-op.
      flt_ctx2's libass track is empty.
   3. Video frames render against flt_ctx2. Empty track -> no cues
      visible. Sidecar SRT subtitles silently lost.
 .
 Embedded subtitles dodge the race because their decoder is paced by
 the same demuxer that feeds video: handle_subtitle keeps firing past
 the rebind, so flt_ctx2's track gets fresh cues from continued
 decoding (patch 0101's "the live graph will see fresh subs as decoding
 resumes" -- true for embedded, false for an instant-EOF sidecar).
 .
 Fix: treat the per-binding queue as the persistent source of truth.
 .
   - handle_subtitle now ALWAYS pending_push()s the chunk, then ALSO
     dispatches it immediately if flt_ctx is bound. Replays of the
     full queue into a freshly-bound flt_ctx see every cue ever
     observed, including those dispatched into a previous (now-freed)
     graph's track.
 .
   - link_graph calls a new pending_replay() (instead of
     pending_drain()) that walks the queue without consuming it. Cap
     and queue lifetime semantics are unchanged; only the
     consume-on-drain step is dropped.
 .
   - pending_drain() is retained but no longer called (kept for
     symmetry / possible future use).
 .
 Memory: ~200 bytes per cue (ass_line is the long field -- typical
 SRT events wrapped in ASS dialog tags are < 80 chars). 2-hour movie
 with 2000 cues = ~400 KiB per binding. Bounded by the existing
 INLINEASS_PENDING_MAX (4096) cap. Freed at uninit (unchanged).
 .
 Bitmap subs (PGS/DVD/DVB/XSUB) are unaffected -- they use the
 replay_bitmap side-channel that drops pre-graph presentations and
 relies on PGS retransmission. Only the text path needs persistent
 replay.
 .
 No rewriter change needed. Restores parity with v1.6.1-and-earlier
 sidecar-SRT prod behavior on the new (orthogonal-detector) shape
 that routes through vf_inlineass HW (VAAPI) branch.
Origin: scaleplex; design ref patch 0101 + post-PR#41 plex-test repro
Forwarded: not-needed
